A||N||5||Luperman||car keeps on dying ...........HELP||||1||
Z||000000||Luperman||05-13-2001||01:35 PM||||I have a 86 V-6 86SE and while trying to charge the A/C up the car shuts off while idling a couple of times  but starts back up no problem so I'm driving it to the store and it dies on me when I pull into a parking spot and does not want to restart until a half an hour goes by.I drive it home and it dies again , so I switch out the distributor module with a spare one it does the same thing , and another thing I noticed is when the engine is cold it takes a good five to ten seconds for it to start where before this happened it cranked right up. so my dilemma is it keeps on dying on me and will not start back up until it cools down some.<BR> <BR>A reman distributor is in the car 3000 miles ago.  <P>------------------<BR>86 fiero SE 2M6        84 Grand Wagoneer 360||||reg||1
Z||000001||87GTZ34||05-13-2001||01:57 PM||||Sounds like your fuel pump relay.  GM put in a fail safe in case the relay fails which is a switch activated by oil pressure.  Here goes: When cold, oil pres builds turns on fuel pump & car starts, slight delay; when hot while idling, oil pressure drops, switch turns off and fuel pump stops.  Cranking won't push oil pres high enough to turn switch for fule pump on until oil cools a bit.  When you turn the ignition to the on position, you should hear the fuel pump kick on for about 2 seconds.  If you don't hear that check the relay - its mounted to the firewall right behind the driver.<P>GL||||reg||1
Z||000002||Luperman||05-13-2001||02:12 PM||||You know in the morning when I 1st start it I watched the oil gauge and when it reaches about 50 psi then it starts . you might be right 87 I will look into that thanks <P>------------------<BR>86 fiero SE 2M6        84 Grand Wagoneer 360||||reg||1
Z||000003||Luperman||05-15-2001||09:46 PM||||I just wanted to say thanks to 87GTZ34 it was the fuel pump relay and my car is happy once more.<P>------------------<BR>86 fiero SE 2M6        84 Grand Wagoneer 360||||reg||10
